  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "yHdJqKW9YZZ7voj1Memj5hEGm1U=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:49:03.892Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The Vetra package ecosystem shipped as one of v6.0.0's five highlights, and its behavioural claims are the ones that matter downstream:\n\n- **Dynamic loading** \u2014 Connect and Switchboard load **processors and subgraphs at runtime** from the HTTP registry, with *no rebuild required* when a new package is published.\n- **Auto-discovery** \u2014 Connect **automatically finds and installs the correct package when it encounters an unknown document type**. That is what makes the registry's `by-document-type` lookup a user-facing feature rather than an API curiosity.\n- **Version picker** \u2014 the Connect UI lets a user choose a specific dist-tag version when installing.\n\nThe CLI surface is three commands against a private, npm-compatible, Verdaccio-backed registry:\n\n```bash\nph publish                                  # publish a built package\nph install @your-org/your-package           # install (Powerhouse registry by default)\nph unpublish @your-org/your-package@1.0.0   # unpublish and purge the CDN cache\n```\n\nTwo related v6 improvements that shape how those packages are built: **separate node and browser processor bundles** (processors publish distinct entrypoints), and tree-shaking work \u2014 `sideEffects: false` in generated boilerplate, with **pglite, jszip and renown crypto lazily loaded**. The last one is the same lazy-import discipline the knowledge-note package needs in production.\n\nOne breaking change from the same release still applies to any project carrying old output: **delete `src/subgraphs/`**, because subgraphs are now generated and loaded at runtime and a checked-in copy conflicts.\n\n## Provenance\n- `apps/academy/docs/academy/ReleaseNotes/index.md` \u2014 v6.0.0 \u203a Vetra Package Ecosystem; Improvements (bundles, tree-shaking); Breaking Changes (delete src/subgraphs)\n\n_Extracted from the Powerhouse repository at **v6.2.2-dev.74**._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-03T07:49:03.892Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:49:03.892Z"
    }
  },
